# Rule 02 hinges on tests/original/test_fuzzy.py being byte-identical to
# upstream. Git's autocrlf would rewrite it on checkout — on Windows the file
# arrives with CRLF, its SHA-256 changes, and it looks modified when it is not.
# `-text` pins the bytes on every platform.
tests/original/test_fuzzy.py -text

# The vendored original C is a reference artifact; leave its bytes alone too.
oracle/double_metaphone.c -text
oracle/double_metaphone.h -text

# Everything we wrote: normalise to LF in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.exe binary
